Anyone else experienced this problem?

I used to run my Macintosh under system 6.0.7 and use Nethack 3.0pl10/
3.0j (whichever you prefer).  Now I'm using a very recent beta-release
of system 7.0, which seems to work fine for about 99% of my other
applications.  Am I the only one experiencing this?  I can't get any
of my characters to live more than 10 minutes (dlvl 3-5) without
nethack crashing severely enough to force a reboot.

I've checked for viruses with Disinfectant2.4, made sure no other
programs are running, and turned on and off all my hokey INIT/CDEVs to
make sure that it wasn't a silly conflict with anything nonstandard.

It doesn't bus error, it actually stops at a _Debugger call (A9FF).  I
can duplicate the situation if someone from the dev team wants more
details about this problem (hardware specs, circumstances surrounding
crashes, etc.)

I hope that the dev team has access to System7.0 for testing...I'm sure
that most Mac users (that have the option) will want to run 7.0 as soon
as possible (it's really nice!).  Hopefully Nethack and System7.0 aren't
mutually exclusive.



